  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Sisters in Science (2006), published by Purdue University, has no recorded citations yet, but it has been downloaded 416 times. Beyond that, it is used in teaching.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Sisters in Science by Diann Jordan was published by Purdue University in 2006. Conceptually, the work connects to Presentation (obstetrics), Presidency, Race (biology), Oral history and Gender studies.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">OpenAlex records no citations for the book so far.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">In teaching, it is discussed in 1 recorded lecture. It has been downloaded 416 times via OAPEN. It is recorded in 5 library collections. Its subject matter aligns with Gender equality among the Sustainable Development Goals.</p>",
